From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SweetSurface: keep the row a client asks for on surfaces that are not BGRA

Every explicit IOSurfaceBytesPerRow was rounded up to 64 bytes for the
GPU's pitch, on the idea that clients take the real row from the lock
result. The CPU code that draws Control Center's glyphs ('LA08' surfaces,
e.g. 105 px in 224 bytes) goes by the row it asked for: drawn with 224,
read with 256, the glyphs came out as sheared stripes. Surfaces that are
not blue-first pixels are always copied into a texture, never shared
with the GPU, so they keep the row they asked for (a multiple of 16).
bluesurf_exactrow=0 rounds every row as before. Each changed row is
logged, the first 24.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
@@ -468,6 +468,36 @@
 static TUNABLE(uint32_t, sweet_surf_wrap, "bluesurf_wrap", 1);  /* 0154: 0 = refuse selector 6 as before */
 
 /*
+ * 0169: an explicit row on a surface that is not blue-first pixels ('LA08' glyphs, 'A008' masks...) stays as asked
+ * (a multiple of 16), not rounded up to 64 (0207-sf-0153). Those surfaces are always copied into a texture, never
+ * shared with the GPU, and the CPU code that draws Control Center's glyphs goes by the row it asked for, not the
+ * lock result: drawn with 224 bytes a row and read with 256, they came out as sheared stripes.
+ * bluesurf_exactrow=0: every row rounded, as before.
+ */
+static TUNABLE(uint32_t, sweet_surf_exactrow, "bluesurf_exactrow", 1);
+
+static void
+sweet_surface_exact_row(SweetSurface *s, OSDictionary *props)
+{
+	uint32_t asked = sweet_dict_u32(props, "IOSurfaceBytesPerRow", 0);
+	if (!sweet_surf_exactrow || asked == 0 || asked == s->bytesPerRow || s->planeCount != 0) {
+		return;
+	}
+	bool keep = (asked & 15u) == 0 && asked < s->bytesPerRow && s->pixelFormat != 0x42475241u /* 'BGRA' */ &&
+	    s->pixelFormat != 0 && asked >= sweet_div_up(s->width, s->elementWidth) * s->bytesPerElement;
+	static uint32_t said;
+	if (said++ < 24) {
+		char fcc[5] = { (char)(s->pixelFormat >> 24), (char)(s->pixelFormat >> 16), (char)(s->pixelFormat >> 8),
+			        (char)s->pixelFormat, 0 };
+		IOLog("SweetSurface: '%s' %u x %u asked for %u bytes a row, given %u: %s\n", fcc, s->width, s->height, asked,
+		    s->bytesPerRow, keep ? "keeping the asked row" : "left rounded");
+	}
+	if (keep) {
+		s->bytesPerRow = asked;
+	}
+}
+
+/*
  * 0154: a surface whose pixels are a range of the caller's own memory (wired
  * while the surface lives; completed in SweetSurface::free), for writing if it
  * can be, else for reading (a picture that is only shown).
@@ -738,6 +768,9 @@
 	}
 	s->parentID = args->scalarInputCount > 0 ? (uint32_t)args->scalarInput[0] : 0;
 	ret = sweet_surface_layout(s, props);
+	if (ret == kIOReturnSuccess) {
+		sweet_surface_exact_row(s, props);
+	}
 	/*
 	 * 0154: IOSurfaceAddress = a surface around memory the caller has already
 	 * (CoreAnimation's GL renderer makes them around app icons and layer contents).
